Goal: when an image file is selected in the tree, the detail pane shows a
preview of it, so I can see what a file is without leaving the explorer.

Context: browser-only, read-only file explorer in plain HTML/CSS/vanilla JS
ES modules, no build step. The detail pane already shows name, size, type,
last modified and dimensions. src/lib/ is pure; src/ui/ does DOM and file
access. Project rules are in CLAUDE.md.

Scope: previews for PNG, JPEG, GIF and WebP, shown above the metadata,
scaled down to fit the pane while keeping the aspect ratio. Folders and
non-image files show no preview area at all. Out of scope: SVG, HEIC, zoom,
thumbnails in the tree, EXIF.

How to approach a few things:
- Use URL.createObjectURL(file) for the image source, because it's local and
  read-only, so it stays within the no-network rule. Revoke the previous URL
  whenever the selection changes, because unreleased blob URLs keep the whole
  file in memory.
- Put the "is this previewable?" decision in src/lib/ as a pure function of
  the MIME type, because that keeps it testable with node --test.
- Use CSS variables from tokens.css for the preview's max height, border and
  background, because styling is only allowed through tokens. Add tokens
  there if you need them.
- When a file fails to decode, show a short "Preview unavailable" line
  instead of a broken image icon, because a broken icon looks like a bug in
  the explorer.

Done when:
- Clicking a PNG, JPEG, GIF or WebP shows its preview; clicking a folder or a
  .txt shows none.
- Selecting several images quickly always ends on the last one selected,
  never an earlier one that loaded late.
- Unit tests cover the previewable-type function, including uppercase MIME
  types and an empty type string.
- `npm run check` passes. Run it yourself and include the result.
- Commit everything, including prompts/ex04-image-preview.md, with message
  "feat(detail): image preview".

If you notice other bugs along the way, list them in your report and don't
fix them. If you found none, say so.

Report: files changed, check result, how I can verify in the browser, and
other bugs noticed.
